    {
      "title": "Path Operations and the Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Path Operations and the Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Path Operation Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Path operation== = method decorator + path + function",
                "`@app.get('/items')` binds a **URL and verb** to a function",
                "Function name and ==docstring== feed the docs",
                "==Type hints== drive everything: source, conversion, validation, docs"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.get(\"/items/{item_id}\")",
                "def read_item(item_id: int, q: str | None = None):",
                "    \"\"\"Fetch one item.\"\"\"",
                "    return {\"item_id\": item_id, \"q\": q}"
              ],
              "note": "item_id from path, q from query"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Where Each Argument Comes From",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Signature clue",
                "Source"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Name in the path template",
                  "{blue:Path param}"
                ],
                [
                  "Plain scalar type (`int`, `str`, `bool`)",
                  "{green:Query param}"
                ],
                [
                  "Pydantic model",
                  "{purple:JSON body}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. def vs async def, and Route Order",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`async def` only when you **await** async libraries",
                "Plain `def` runs in a ==threadpool==, so blocking calls do not freeze the loop",
                "`async def` with blocking code stalls the whole event loop"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.get(\"/users/me\")",
                "def me(): ...",
                "@app.get(\"/users/{user_id}\")",
                "def user(user_id: int): ..."
              ],
              "note": "fixed route first"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Path order matters",
              "text": "Declare `/users/me` **before** `/users/{user_id}`, or 'me' is parsed as an id and fails validation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Path and Query Parameters",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Path and Query Parameters",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Path vs Query",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Param",
                "Declared as",
                "Required?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Path",
                  "name inside `{item_id}`",
                  "{red:always}"
                ],
                [
                  "Query",
                  "argument not in path, no default",
                  "{red:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Query + default",
                  "`limit: int = 10`",
                  "{green:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "Optional query",
                  "`q: str | None = None`",
                  "{green:no}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`item_id: int` parses the path; `/items/abc` returns ==422==",
                "`bool` accepts ==true/1/on/yes== and arrives as a real `bool`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Constraints",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Path(ge=1, le=1000)` bounds a number",
                "`Query(max_length=50, pattern='^a')` checks a string",
                "==Annotated== is the modern style: `Annotated[int, Query(ge=1)]`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.get(\"/items/{item_id}\")",
                "async def read(",
                "    item_id: Annotated[int, Path(ge=1, le=1000)],",
                "    q: Annotated[str | None, Query(max_length=50)] = None,",
                "    limit: Annotated[int, Query(ge=1)] = 10): ..."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. List Query Params",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A list needs ==Query()== explicitly",
                "`?tags=a&tags=b` fills the list"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "tags: Annotated[list[str], Query()] = []"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistake",
              "text": "Without `Query()`, a `list` parameter is treated as a **body**, not a query string."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Request Bodies with Pydantic v2",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Request Bodies with Pydantic v2",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Body = a BaseModel",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Param typed as a ==BaseModel== subclass → read as **JSON body**",
                "FastAPI validates it and hands you an `Item` instance",
                "No default → ==required==; None-able still needs `= None`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class Item(BaseModel):",
                "    name: str",
                "    price: float",
                "    tags: list[str] = []",
                "    note: str | None = None",
                "",
                "@app.post(\"/items\")",
                "async def create(item: Item): ..."
              ],
              "note": "name and price required"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pydantic v2 names",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "v1 (gone)",
                "v2"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`.dict()`",
                  "`model_dump()`"
                ],
                [
                  "`parse_obj()`",
                  "`model_validate()`"
                ],
                [
                  "PATCH partial",
                  "`model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mixing sources",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Path + query + body in ==one function== works",
                "Two model params → JSON keyed by **param name**",
                "`Body(embed=True)` wraps one model the same way: `{\"item\": {...}}`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bare `dict` body: no validation, no docs",
                "GET with a body: discouraged",
                "Plain-class mutable default is shared; use `Field(default_factory=list)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Type the body as a ==model==, not `dict`. In v2 use **model_** methods."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Validation with Field and Errors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Validation with Field and Errors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Field() Constraints",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Field()` adds ==constraints== and docs metadata inside a model"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class Item(BaseModel):",
                "    name: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=50)",
                "    price: float = Field(gt=0, description='USD')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Constraints"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Numbers",
                  "`gt` `ge` `lt` `le`"
                ],
                [
                  "Strings",
                  "`min_length` `max_length` `pattern`"
                ],
                [
                  "Docs",
                  "`examples=` `description=`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Custom Checks (v2)",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@field_validator('name')` on a ==classmethod==: one field",
                "`@model_validator(mode='after')`: ==cross-field== rules",
                "v1 `@validator` is {red:gone}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "JSON body",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "sub": "Field + validators",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "422 Unprocessable Entity",
                    "sub": "detail: [{loc, msg, type}]",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "v2 does not coerce loosely: `'1.5'` is never silently an `int`",
                "`Optional[str]` without `= None` is still ==required=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Reading loc",
              "text": "`loc` shows ==where== the error is, e.g. `['body','price']`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "response_model and Status Codes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "response_model and Status Codes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Filtering the Output",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`response_model=UserOut` ==filters and validates== the returned data",
                "Secrets like {red:password} never leave, even if you return the full object",
                "Pattern: ==UserIn== (with password) and ==UserOut== (without)",
                "Return annotation `-> UserOut` does the same job"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class UserIn(BaseModel):",
                "    name: str",
                "    password: str",
                "class UserOut(BaseModel):",
                "    name: str",
                "@app.post(\"/users\", status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)",
                "async def create(u: UserIn) -> UserOut:",
                "    return u"
              ],
              "note": "password is dropped from the response"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Shape and Status",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Option",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`response_model_exclude_unset=True`",
                  "drops unset defaults"
                ],
                [
                  "`response_model_exclude_none=True`",
                  "drops nulls"
                ],
                [
                  "`response_model=list[Item]`",
                  "a collection"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`status_code` goes on the ==decorator==",
                "{green:201} create, {orange:204} delete with ==no body==",
                "`status.HTTP_201_CREATED` reads better than a bare number"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.get(\"/items/{id}\", responses={404: {\"description\": \"Not found\"}})",
                "def read(id: int):",
                "    if id not in db:",
                "        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Item not found\")",
                "    return db[id]"
              ],
              "note": "raise sends the error; responses= only documents it"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`responses={404: ...}` is for the ==docs only==. You still must `raise HTTPException`."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Does returning the full user leak password?** No, `response_model` filters it.",
                "**Body on 204?** None, return nothing.",
                "**Does `responses=` raise a 404?** No, docs only."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
